# Feature Planning

## Required cycle

Medium/large features: **Specify → Design → Tasks → Execute**.

- Planning: skill `vitals-spec-driven` + agent `planner-feature`
- Requirement IDs: prefix **`HOTSPOT-*`** in `spec.md` / `tasks.md`

## Session boundary

Planning stops at Tasks with `tasks.md` **Status: `Planned`** — no Execute in the same session.

| Actor | While Status is `Draft` / `Planned` | Hook |
| ----- | ---------------------------------- | ---- |
| `planner-feature` | Never edits `src/`, `bin/`, `tests/` | `deny` |
| Main agent | Does not implement under `src/`, `bin/`, `tests/` without explicit user confirmation | `ask` |

Neither starts `orchestrator-implementer` nor runs Execute phases while Status is `Draft`/`Planned` — promote Status in a **new** session, then Execute. After the user confirms, quick mode (**≤3 files**) stays the only in-session implementation escape hatch.

Details: [planning-session-boundary.md](../skills/vitals-spec-driven/references/planning-session-boundary.md); quick mode: [quick-mode.md](../skills/vitals-spec-driven/references/quick-mode.md).

## Execute

- Playbook: [execute-orchestration-playbook.md](../skills/vitals-execute/references/execute-orchestration-playbook.md) (phases **A→F**); skill `vitals-execute`
- Agent: `orchestrator-implementer` in a **separate** session after promoting Status
- Final project gate: `verifier-quality-gates` (Phase **E**) — see [quality-gates.mdc](quality-gates.mdc)

## Requirement sources

- Design SoT: `.specs/codebase/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Ownership: `.specs/codebase/DOC-OWNERSHIP.md`
- Feature specs: `.specs/features/<feature>/`
- Milestones / decisions: `ROADMAP.md` / `STATE.md`

## Validation (CLI)

No interactive UAT. Per-task gates + project gate + skill `vitals-cli-validation` when flags/pipeline change. Exit codes: [docs/cli-reference.md](../../docs/cli-reference.md#exit-codes).
